-- infra/e2e/seed/40-phase2-batch2-fixture.sql.tmpl
--
-- Phase 2 batch 2 (mig-infra) — data-point parity fixture for the three
-- NEW page-pairs this batch covers: /analytics (tabs overview/advanced/crm/
-- account), /activity-logs, /loyalty-members. Applied AFTER
-- 30-phase2-batch1-fixture.sql.tmpl (already piped into the SAME app/tenant
-- DB by parity.mjs's seedDatabase()) — reuses batch-1's `users`/`messages`/
-- `orders`/`transactions`/`user_tags`/`user_tag_assignments` rows wherever
-- the query being tested is unscoped by line_account_id (see the "WHY NO
-- line_accounts ROWS" note below), and adds NEW tables/rows batch-1 never
-- touched. Deliberately a NEW numbered file (not appended to 30-*, not
-- reusing 15-/10-) for the exact reason batch-1's own 15- file gave for not
-- reusing run.mjs's 10-: different purpose (a different batch's fixture),
-- avoid collision — see docs/runbooks/phase2-batch1-users-dashboard-parity.md
-- §1 step 2 for that precedent.
--
-- No USE statement of its own — same convention as 20-/30-: the caller
-- (parity.mjs's seedDatabase()) prepends `USE \`<app-db>\`;`.
--
-- DETERMINISM: every timestamp is a MySQL relative-date expression
-- (NOW()/CURDATE()/DATE_SUB(...)), never a wall-clock literal — same
-- reasoning as 30-*'s own header comment.
--
-- ===========================================================================
-- WHY NO `line_accounts` ROWS (read before adding any — this is the single
-- most important constraint on this file, verified by reading
-- includes/header.php lines 138-172, classes/AdminAuth.php's
-- getAccessibleBots()/getCurrentBotId(), and packages/auth/src/session.ts):
--
-- PHP's includes/header.php (required by EVERY protected admin page,
-- including analytics.php/activity-logs.php/loyalty-members.php) contains a
-- currentBotId AUTO-SELECT fallback: the FIRST time header.php runs for a
-- session with no `$_SESSION['current_bot_id']` set yet, if
-- getAccessibleBots() returns ANY row (which it does the instant
-- `line_accounts` has ANY `is_active=1` row and the admin is super_admin —
-- our seeded e2e admin IS super_admin), header.php auto-selects that bot and
-- WRITES it into `$_SESSION['current_bot_id']` — permanently, for the rest
-- of that PHP session (every subsequent page fetch in the same phpSid).
--
-- Next's session (packages/auth/src/session.ts line ~172) has NO equivalent
-- auto-select: `login()` always sets `currentBotId: null`, and the ONLY way
-- it ever becomes non-null is an explicit `switchBot()` call — which
-- apps/admin does not yet wire into any UI (verified: no `switch_bot`/
-- `switchBot(` call site under apps/admin/src, confirmed by grep).
--
-- Consequence: if this file seeded even ONE `line_accounts` row, the VERY
-- FIRST PHP page fetch in parity.mjs's shared phpSid session (which is
-- `users:baseline`, batch-1's own first entry — run before any of this
-- batch's new entries) would silently auto-select a real bot ID into
-- $_SESSION for the ENTIRE REST OF THE RUN, while Next's session stays null
-- forever. Several of batch-1's ALREADY-PASSING queries
-- (includes/dashboard/crm.php's `(line_account_id = ? OR ? IS NULL)`
-- PARAM-nullness pattern — see extract.mjs's FIXTURE_TAG_NAMES section) would
-- then silently re-scope to `line_account_id = <that bot>` on PHP while
-- staying unscoped on Next — a false FAIL (or worse, a false PASS on
-- different underlying data) for entries that have NOTHING to do with this
-- batch's pages. This is a hard, cross-batch correctness hazard, not a
-- style preference — this file MUST NOT seed `line_accounts`,
-- `account_followers`, `account_events`, or `account_daily_stats` (the
-- account-tab tables, which are unreachable without a real line_accounts row
-- anyway — see the "account" tab note below).
--
-- Net effect (FLAGGED FINDING for the build report, not fixed here — out of
-- this agent's allowed paths, which are infra-only):
--   - analytics.php's overview/advanced/crm tabs use the
--     `(line_account_id = ? OR line_account_id IS NULL)` COLUMN-nullness
--     pattern (overview.php, crm.php) or a plain "$this->lineAccountId ?
--     filter : no filter" truthy check (AnalyticsModel.php, the 'advanced'
--     tab) — BOTH evaluate to "every row with line_account_id IS NULL" (or
--     literally every row, for the truthy-check tables) whenever
--     $lineAccountId/currentBotId is null, which it always is here. So this
--     file seeds every new analytics row with `line_account_id = NULL` and
--     they show up correctly on BOTH stacks.
--   - loyalty-members.php/queries.ts gate their ENTIRE query behind
--     `if ($lineAccountId > 0)` / `session.currentBotId ?? 0`. With no
--     line_accounts row, lineAccountId is ALWAYS 0 on BOTH stacks, so the
--     query never runs at all — stats stay {total:0,points:0,today:0},
--     members stay []. The `users` rows seeded below (`line_user_id LIKE
--     'offline:%'`) are written for completeness per this batch's brief
--     ("loyalty-tier/points rows matching loyalty-members.php's actual
--     query") and to enable a future harness that DOES wire up a bot
--     switch, but are INERT in this run — the loyalty-members parity
--     entries verify the (still perfectly real and meaningful) "zero bots
--     selected -> empty state" equality, not a populated list. See
--     docs/runbooks's Phase 2 batch 2 section for the full writeup.
--   - analytics.php's "account" tab (สถิติแยกตามบอท) is INHERENTLY about
--     per-bot stats; with zero `line_accounts` rows it legitimately renders
--     the "กรุณาเลือกบอทเพื่อดูสถิติ" (please select a bot) prompt on a real
--     production tenant that hasn't set up a LINE OA yet, too — this is not
--     a fixture gap, it's a real, valid, testable state. No account_* rows
--     seeded; the account-tab parity entry verifies that prompt state.
-- ===========================================================================

-- ===========================================================================
-- 1) activity_logs (55 rows) — exercises activity-logs.php's `type`, `action`,
--    `search`, `date_from`/`date_to` filter branches (queries.ts's buildWhere/
--    countLogs, ported 1:1 from classes/ActivityLogger.php lines 216-304).
--
--    FLAGGED FINDING: classes/AdminAuth.php::login() (lines 173-183) calls
--    ActivityLogger::logAuth(ACTION_LOGIN, ...) on every successful PHP
--    login — so parity.mjs's own `phpLogin()` call adds ONE extra
--    log_type='auth'/action='login' row to `activity_logs` AFTER this file
--    seeds it. `internal/session-bridge.php`'s 'login-sync' action (what
--    Next's `nextLogin()` bridge-sync hits) only assigns raw `$_SESSION`
--    keys (verified by reading the full file) — it does NOT call
--    ActivityLogger. Net: PHP's activity_logs table has ONE MORE row than
--    Next's for the rest of the run — a genuine backend asymmetry (Next's
--    login() has no activity-log side effect PHP's does), not a fixture or
--    extraction bug. WORKAROUND (not a fix — apps/admin/**, classes/**,
--    packages/auth/** are all out of this agent's allowed paths): every row
--    below is dated 2-21 days in the past (NEVER "today"), and every
--    activity-logs parity entry in parity.mjs applies a `date_to` bound of
--    "yesterday" (computed at run time, never hardcoded) so the PHP-only
--    login row — always dated "today" — is excluded from every comparison.
--    Flagged for mig-orchestrator: a future ticket may want `@reya/auth`'s
--    login() to also write an activity_logs row for real audit-trail parity
--    in production, independent of this harness.
--
--    3 rows contain the literal marker "BATCH2SEARCHMARK" for the `search`
--    filter test (queries.ts's search clause: description/user_name/
--    admin_name LIKE). The remaining 52 rows cycle through all 11 log_types
--    (auth/user/admin/data/consent/message/order/pharmacy/ai/api/system —
--    the exact keys activity-logs.php's own $logTypes array uses) x all 10
--    actions (create/read/update/delete/login/logout/export/send/approve/
--    reject — activity-logs.php's own $actions array), so every filter
--    dropdown option has real, non-empty matches. `action=login` (i%10==4)
--    hits exactly 6 rows, used by the `action` filter test. `type=pharmacy`
--    hits 6 rows (5 cyclic + 1 marker), used by the `type` filter test.
--    `type=consent AND action=login` hits exactly 1 row, used by the
--    `combined` filter test. All spread 2-21 days ago so the wide
--    date_from=25d-ago/date_to=yesterday bound (used by every entry, see
--    above) includes all 55 rows.
-- ===========================================================================
